Ingredients:
- 240g Sourdough Discard (unfed, room temperature)
- 2 Cups (250 g) All Purpose Flour
- 1 tbsp Baking Powder
- 1/2 tsp baking soda
- 1 tsp Salt
- 1/2 Cup ( 1 stick/113 g) cold unsalted butter, cubed
- 1/3 cup cold milk or buttermilk (as needed for dough consistency)

Instructions:
-Pre-Heat Oven to 425 F, line a baking sheet with parchment paper
- In a large bowl, whisk together flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt
- add cold cubed butter and use a pastry cutter or your fingers to mix
until it forms pea-sized crumbs
- stir in sourdough discard and just enough cold milk/ buttermilk to form
soft dough that holds together but isn't sticky
- turn the dough onto a lightly floured surface, gently pat into a 1 inch
thick rectangle.
- Fold it in half once or twice (this creates layers), then cut out
biscuits with a round cutter or cup.
- Place biscuits on the prepared sheet, touching slightly for soft sides or
spaced apart for crisp edges.
- Bake for 12-15 minutes or until golden brown.
- For extra rise, chill the cut biscuits in the fridge for 10 minutes
before baking.

